Subject: hqrii.f: never return an all-zero column for a degenerate root

A defect in MOPAC 7's own eigensolver, not in the translation and not in the
wasm build. It is present in 7.00 and in 7.01, on every target. THIS PATCH
DEVIATES FROM THE 1993 SOURCE: it adds a test and a recovery pass that the
original does not have.

WHAT IT FIXES
  HQRII finds eigenvectors by inverse iteration, one root at a time, and
  Gram-Schmidts each one against the roots it has already accepted at the same
  eigenvalue ("RE-ORTHOGONALISATION", label 400-420). For a degenerate pair the
  shift of the second root equals the shift of the first to within one ulp, so
  the LU of (T - shift*I) is singular to working precision: its smallest pivot
  IS rounding noise, and the back substitution then returns a direction fixed
  by the factorisation rather than by the start vector. Both roots come back
  as the same vector, the Gram-Schmidt subtracts the whole of the second one,
  and what reaches the normalisation is a residue of about 1.D-19 per element.

  Nothing reports that. The normalisation is

      430 SUM=1.D-24
          DO 440 J=1,N
      440 SUM=SUM+V(J,I)**2
          SINV=1.D0/SQRT(SUM)

  and with the residue at ~1.D-38 the 1.D-24 floor is the whole sum, so SINV
  comes out 1.D12 where it should have been ~1.D19 and the column leaves with
  a norm of 9.8e-08 instead of 1. MOPAC prints it as all zeros, and SYMTRZ's
  character test (R00011 rejects a column whose self-overlap is below 1.D-5)
  then labels the whole degenerate set '????' instead of, here, 1PI:

    AM1 hydrogen fluoride, wasm, before        and after / both native builds
                1 SI    2 SI   3 ????  4 ????        1 SI    2 SI    1 PI   1 PI
      Py F 1    .0000   .0000   .0000   .0000        .0000   .0000   .0000 -1.0000
      Pz F 1    .0000   .0000  1.0000   .0000        .0000   .0000  1.0000  .0000

  Eigenvalues are not affected: the QR half of HQRII is untouched by this and
  every level matches a native build exactly, before and after.

  It is NOT a wasm defect, although that is where it was found. Over a
  201-point bond-length scan of HF, HCl, N2 and CO under MNDO, AM1 and PM3 --
  2412 geometries through each build -- the shipped wasm lost a vector at 146
  of them (6.1%) and a native build of the identical C at 43 (1.8%); the
  Ghemical MOPAC 7.01 binary prints the same empty column at AM1 HF r=1.05 and
  PM3 HCl r=1.30. The two targets differ only in which geometries fall in,
  because arm64 clang contracts a*b+c into fmadd in the Householder reduction
  and the wasm MVP has no f64 FMA opcode, so the last bits of the tridiagonal
  differ and a different pivot is taken. The hole in the algorithm is the same
  on both. After this patch: 0 of 2412 on each.

WHAT IT DOES
  1. Detects the collapse, which the original never does: if SUM at label 430
     is below 1.D-20 the vector is not an eigenvector. Label 300 scales the
     largest element to EPS1=1.D-5 and the back transformation is orthogonal,
     so SUM is about 1.D-10 for any vector that survived. Measured over the 42
     verification decks, every SUM is either at the 1.D-24 floor (annihilated)
     or 1.D-15 and above; 1.D-20 separates the two by four orders on one side
     and five on the other.
  2. Runs the inverse iteration once more for that root, from THE SAME start
     vector (RN is saved and restored, so the pseudo-random stream is not
     advanced and every later root is bit-for-bit unchanged), with two
     additions that are what LAPACK's DSTEIN does on every pass:
       * the start vector, and the vector after each pass, are projected out
         of the directions the set has already accepted. Those are kept in
         VTRI in the TRIDIAGONAL basis, which is the basis the iteration works
         in, so they are copied at label 330 before the back transformation.
       * the shift is displaced by 1.D-12*GERSCH. Projecting alone is not
         enough: with the shift exactly at the root the solve returns one
         direction whatever the start vector, because the pivot is noise.
         Displaced far above that noise and far below the gap to the next
         distinct root, the whole set is amplified by the same 1/PTOL and the
         direction is the start vector's again. GERSCH is HQRII's own
         Gershgorin bound, so this scales with the matrix.
  The degeneracy-group test that was at label 380 is hoisted to the top of the
  loop, unchanged, because the start vector now has to know the group; nothing
  between the two points alters E or IG. V(*,M) holds the tridiagonal diagonal
  and the loop overwrites it while reading it when I reaches M, which one pass
  survives but a second would not, so it is copied into TDIAG first.

  The healthy path does no arithmetic it did not do before: same start vector,
  same shift (SHIFT=E(I) exactly), same 1.D-24 floor, same order of operations.
  Measured: of the 42 verification decks, 39 produce a byte-identical listing
  and the 3 that change are the three hydrogen-fluoride decks, each of which
  had an all-zero column (AM1 in the final EIGENVECTORS block, MNDO and PM3 on
  SCF iteration 1) and now has a unit vector there.

  Cost: +796 bytes of .wasm raw, +200 gzip, -333 brotli; run time unchanged
  within the noise of the machine (the added work is one norm and one scaled
  copy of N elements per eigenvector, against the O(N**3) Householder).

--- a/hqrii.f
+++ b/hqrii.f
@@ -19,6 +19,7 @@
 *
 ************************************************************************
       DIMENSION W(5,MAXPAR)
+      DIMENSION TDIAG(MAXORB), VTRI(MAXORB,MAXORB)
       IF(N.LE.1 .OR. M .LE.1 .OR. M .GT. N) THEN
          IF(N.EQ.1 .AND. M.EQ.1) THEN
             E(1)=A(1)
@@ -160,15 +161,55 @@
       RA=EPS*0.6180339887485D0
 C    0.618... IS THE FIBONACCI NUMBER (-1+SQRT(5))/2.
       IG=1
+      NVT=0
+      DO 225 J=1,N
+  225 TDIAG(J)=V(J,M)
       DO 450 I=1,M
          IM1=I-1
+C
+C   Which set of (near-)degenerate roots is root I in? This test was at
+C   label 380, after the back transformation; it is hoisted here so
+C   that a recovery pass knows which directions the set already holds.
+C   Nothing between here and 380 alters E or IG.
+C
+         DO 205 J=IG,I
+            IF(ABS(E(J)-E(I)) .LT. EPS2) GOTO 206
+  205    CONTINUE
+         J=I
+  206    IG=J
+         IF(IG .EQ. I) NVT=0
+         LFIX=0
+         RNKEEP=RN
+  207    RN=RNKEEP
+C
+C   A recovery pass also has to move the shift off the eigenvalue. With
+C   the shift AT a degenerate root, the pivot of (T-shift*I) in the
+C   two-dimensional set is rounding noise, and the back substitution
+C   then returns one direction fixed by the factorisation whatever the
+C   start vector is -- projecting the start vector alone changes
+C   nothing. Displaced by PTOL, which is far above that noise and far
+C   below the gap to the next distinct root, the whole set is amplified
+C   by the same 1/PTOL, so the direction is the start vector's again.
+C   LAPACK's DSTEIN separates close shifts the same way.
+C
+         SHIFT=E(I)
+         IF(LFIX .NE. 0) SHIFT=SHIFT+1.D-12*MAX(GERSCH,1.D0)
          DO 230 J=1,N
             W(3,J)=0.D0
             W(4,J)=W(1,J)
-            W(5,J)=V(J,M)-E(I)
+            W(5,J)=TDIAG(J)-SHIFT
             RN=RN+RA
             IF(RN.GE.EPS) RN=RN-EPS
   230    V(J,I)=RN
+         IF(LFIX .EQ. 0) GOTO 236
+         DO 235 KV=1,NVT
+            TSUM=0.D0
+            DO 232 J=1,N
+  232       TSUM=TSUM+VTRI(J,KV)*V(J,I)
+            DO 233 J=1,N
+  233       V(J,I)=V(J,I)-TSUM*VTRI(J,KV)
+  235    CONTINUE
+  236    CONTINUE
          DO 260 J=1,NM1
             IF(ABS(W(5,J)).GE.ABS(W(1,J))) GOTO 240
             W(2,J)=-W(5,J)/W(1,J)
@@ -205,10 +246,35 @@
   300       S=EPS1/VN
             DO 310 J=1,N
   310       V(J,I)=V(J,I)*S
-            IF(ITERE.GT.1 .AND. VN.GT.1) GOTO 330
+            IF(LFIX .EQ. 0) GOTO 316
+            DO 315 KV=1,NVT
+               TSUM=0.D0
+               DO 312 J=1,N
+  312          TSUM=TSUM+VTRI(J,KV)*V(J,I)
+               DO 313 J=1,N
+  313          V(J,I)=V(J,I)-TSUM*VTRI(J,KV)
+  315       CONTINUE
+  316       IF(ITERE.GT.1 .AND. VN.GT.1) GOTO 330
   320    CONTINUE
 C     TRANSFORMATION OF EIGENVECTORS
-  330    IF(N.EQ.2) GOTO 380
+C
+C   V(*,I) is still in the tridiagonal basis here, which is the basis the
+C   inverse iteration works in, so this is where a recovery pass needs the
+C   directions its set has already taken. Keeping them costs one copy per
+C   root and changes no arithmetic.
+C
+  330    IF(NVT .GE. MAXORB) GOTO 336
+         TNORM=0.D0
+         DO 331 J=1,N
+  331    TNORM=TNORM+V(J,I)**2
+         IF(TNORM .GT. 1.D-30) GOTO 333
+         DO 332 J=1,N
+  332    VTRI(J,NVT+1)=0.D0
+         GOTO 336
+  333    TNORM=1.D0/SQRT(TNORM)
+         DO 334 J=1,N
+  334    VTRI(J,NVT+1)=V(J,I)*TNORM
+  336    IF(N.EQ.2) GOTO 380
          KRANK=NM2*(N+1)/2
          KPIV=NM2*NM1/2
          DO 370 K=NM2,1,-1
@@ -224,12 +290,7 @@
   350       V(KK,I)=A(KRANK)*S+V(KK,I)
   360       KPIV=KPIV-K
   370    KRANK=KRANK-KP1
-  380    DO 390 J=IG,I
-            IF(ABS(E(J)-E(I)) .LT. EPS2) GOTO 400
-  390    CONTINUE
-         J=I
-  400    IG=J
-         IF(IG .EQ. I) GOTO 430
+  380    IF(IG .EQ. I) GOTO 430
 C     RE-ORTHOGONALISATION
          DO 420 K=IG,IM1
             SUM=0.D0
@@ -242,8 +303,28 @@
   430    SUM=1.D-24
          DO 440 J=1,N
   440    SUM=SUM+V(J,I)**2
-         SINV=1.D0/SQRT(SUM)
-         DO 450 J=1,N
-  450 V(J,I)=V(J,I)*SINV
+C
+C   A vector that leaves the re-orthogonalisation with no length left is
+C   not an eigenvector: the inverse iteration returned a direction this
+C   set already holds, and all that is left is rounding noise, which the
+C   1.D-24 floor above then scales up to a norm of about 1.D-7 without
+C   saying anything. Label 300 scales the largest element to EPS1=1.D-5
+C   and the back transformation is orthogonal, so SUM is about 1.D-10 for
+C   any vector that survived. Measured over the 42 verification decks,
+C   every SUM is either at the 1.D-24 floor (the annihilated ones) or
+C   1.D-15 and above, so 1.D-20 separates them by four orders on one side
+C   and five on the other. Run the iteration once more, from the same
+C   start vector, held out of the directions the set already holds --
+C   which is what LAPACK's DSTEIN does on every pass.
+C
+         IF(SUM .GE. 1.D-20) GOTO 442
+         IF(NVT .LE. 0 .OR. LFIX .NE. 0) GOTO 442
+         LFIX=1
+         GOTO 207
+  442    SINV=1.D0/SQRT(SUM)
+         DO 445 J=1,N
+  445    V(J,I)=V(J,I)*SINV
+         IF(NVT .LT. MAXORB) NVT=NVT+1
+  450 CONTINUE
       RETURN
       END
